  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of integrated lifesaving responses to populations affected by displacement and famine in Sharia, East Darfur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtThrough this project, Alight will work with it&apos;s partnernbspAAO and launch a comprehensive response that integrate WASH, Health, Nutrition, GP, GBV, CP, and SNFI targeting Sharia. This project aims to provide integrated response for IDPs and host communities in Sharia. The emergency response will be implemented in coordination with the State Ministry of Health, the state water ministry, local partners including AAO, and project beneficiaries. In response to this vast humanitarian need in Sudan, ALIGHT proposed 12-month Project. The objective is to provide integrated lifesaving services for conflict-affected and vulnerable people in the East Darfur state, Sharia locality. The project will address the immediate needs of affected people, targeting 64,584 people who will be covered through integrated essential lifesaving Health, Nutrition, WASH, protection and ES/NFI services. Health activities will include providing essential medical supplies, establishing mobile clinics, and training healthcare workers to ensure primary healthcare delivery. Special focus will be placed on maternal and child health, vaccination campaigns, and managing common diseases.ltbrgtNutrition efforts will address malnutrition through therapeutic and supplementary feeding programs for children and pregnant and lactating women. Nutrition education sessions will improve community knowledge and practices regarding healthy diets and infant feeding.ltbrgtProtection activities will focus on identifying and supporting vulnerable groups, including women, children, and persons with disabilities. This will involve establishing safe spaces, providing psychosocial support, and implementing community-based protection strategies to enhance resilience and safety.ltbrgtWASH (Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene) initiatives will improve access to clean water by rehabilitating water points and distributing water purification tablets. Sanitation facilities will be constructed or repaired, and hygiene promotion campaigns will reduce the risk of waterborne diseases.ltbrgtBy addressing these critical needs, the project aims to improve the overall well-being of IDPs and host communities in Sharia, ensuring access to essential services and support during this crisis. Alight will implement Health, nutrition, WASH and Protection interventions, while AAO will implement the shelter and ESNFI component of this response.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
